From: Martin Blumenstingl <martin.blumenstingl@googlemail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: add Meson8/8b/8m2 VPU and HDMI support

Port the Meson8/8b/8m2 VPU, HDMI transmitter, VCLK and HDMI PHY
enablement patches (originally from the linux-meson and Armbian 6.12
trees) to Linux 7.3.1, and enable HDMI on the Xunlei OneCloud.

Changes relative to the original series:
- adapt the DRM bridge atomic_enable/atomic_disable callbacks, the
  bridge attach/detect callbacks, the HDMI codec get_dai_id callback,
  the color format flags and the fbdev setup to the 7.3.1 DRM APIs
- allocate the TranSwitch HDMI bridge with devm_drm_bridge_alloc():
  7.3.1's drm_bridge_add() requires a bridge allocated by that helper
  and crashes on a zero-initialised embedded struct drm_bridge
- restore #address-cells/#size-cells/ranges on the HHI syscon node so
  the HDMI TX PHY child device gets a translated MMIO resource
- express the HDMI PHY frequency limits in Hz (7.3.1 uses Hz, not kHz)
- pass the VCLK frequencies in Hz to clk_set_rate_exclusive()
- drop the CVBS DAC PHY changes: the CVBS DAC driver is not part of
  this tree and HDMI does not depend on it
